# The ntfy notification channel, as code.
#
# UNDOCUMENTED BUT VERIFIED (2026-10-15): AutoKuma's docs show notifications
# only as Docker labels, and this stack runs file-only
# (AUTOKUMA__DOCKER__ENABLED=false, deliberately — no second holder of
# docker.sock). The file source turns out to handle them anyway: dropping a
# `type = "notification"` file in here created one, updated it on edit, and
# DELETED it when the file was removed. So no label mode and no docker.sock.
#
# THE FILENAME IS THE ID. Monitors reference this as
# `notification_name_list = ["ntfy"]` — the AutoKuma id, NOT the display `name`
# below. Referencing the display name fails to resolve, and an unresolvable
# name makes AutoKuma DELETE the monitor rather than warn (measured: monitor
# #14 was deleted and came back as #15 with no heartbeat history).
#
# PRIORITIES: 5 for failures, 3 for recoveries. Read from Kuma's own provider
# (server/notification-providers/ntfy.js) rather than inferred from the field
# names, because getting it backwards would silence FAILURES:
#
#   let priority = notification.ntfyPriority || 4;        <- the BASE, used on UP
#   if (status === DOWN) priority = notification.ntfyPriorityDown || ...
#
# So ntfyPriority is the recovery/base priority and ntfyPriorityDown is the
# failure one. Both were 5 — ntfy's max, which bypasses Do Not Disturb — so a
# single flap paged twice at maximum urgency, which MONITORING.md calls the road
# to a muted channel. Failures stay at 5. Recoveries drop to 3 (ntfy's default):
# still delivered, no longer breaking through silent mode.
#
# Note line 57 of that provider: Kuma's "Test" button sends at ntfyPriority, the
# BASE. So a test send now arrives at 3, not 5 — that is expected, not a fault.
#
# The topic IS the credential on ntfy.sh with auth `none` — readable AND
# publishable by anyone holding it — so it is a Tier-2 secret and arrives via
# envsubst from NTFY_TOPIC in the root .env, exactly like the push tokens.
type = "notification"
name = "CoralStack ntfy"
active = true
is_default = true
config = '{"type":"ntfy","name":"CoralStack ntfy","ntfyserverurl":"https://ntfy.sh","ntfytopic":"${NTFY_TOPIC}","ntfyAuthenticationMethod":"none","ntfyPriority":3,"ntfyPriorityDown":5,"ntfyUseTemplate":false,"isDefault":true,"applyExisting":false}'
